  planner_response {
    response: "### MediVoice AI \342\200\224 Phase 1: Backend Foundation & Database Design\n\nPhase 1 for **Aarogya One Hospital** has been designed, implemented, and verified with **26/26 automated tests passing**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Implemented Architecture & File Deliverables\n\n```\nbackend/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.py                     # FastAPI server, CORS middleware, OpenAPI docs at /docs\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 core/config.py              # Pydantic v2 settings & database URL management\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 db/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 base.py                 # DeclarativeBase definition\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 session.py              # Engine lifecycle, connection pooling & get_db dependency\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 models/                     # SQLAlchemy 2.x PostgreSQL-compatible models\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hospital.py             # Aarogya One Hospital\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 department.py           # Clinical departments (Cardiology, Neurology, etc.)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 doctor.py               # Doctor profiles with specialty indexing\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 appointment_slot.py     # Slot availability & uq_doctor_slot_start_time\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 appointment.py          # Atomic booking with UNIQUE(slot_id) constraint\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 lab_order.py            # Workflow metadata (Pending, Processing, Completed, Delayed)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 workflow_exception.py   # Operational exception tracking & resolution note\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 audit_event.py          # Immutable audit logging\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 schemas/                    # Pydantic request & response models\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hospital.py, doctor.py, appointment.py, lab_order.py, workflow.py\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 __init__.py\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/                   # Business layer & AI Tool functions\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 doctor_service.py       # Doctor retrieval & AI tools: search_doctors, get_available_slots\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 appointment_service.py  # Atomic booking, cancellation & AI tool: book_appointment\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 lab_service.py          # Lab order workflow state management\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 workflow_service.py     # Deterministic overdue order detection & exception handling\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/v1/                     # FastAPI route handlers\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hospitals.py, doctors.py, appointments.py, lab_orders.py, workflow.py\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 router.py               # Combined v1 API router\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tests/                          # Pytest test suite (26 passing tests)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 conftest.py                 # TestClient fixture with isolated SQLite in-memory DB\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 test_doctors.py             # 8 tests: queries, filtering, slots & AI tools\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 test_appointments.py        # 10 tests: atomic booking, double booking rejection, cancel, follow-up\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 test_lab_orders.py          # 4 tests: status transitions, validation rejection\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 test_workflow.py            # 4 tests: deterministic detection, assignment, resolution\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 scripts/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 seed_data.py                # Idempotent synthetic seeder for Aarogya One Hospital\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 alembic/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 env.py, script.py.mako\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 versions/0001_initial_schema.py  # Migration establishing all 8 tables & constraints\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 alembic.ini, requirements.txt, .env.example, README.md\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/App.tsx                     # Interactive Developer & Architecture Verification Portal\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Database Schema & Booking Invariants\n\n- **Anti-Double Booking**: The `appointments` table enforces a database-level unique constraint on `slot_id` (`uq_appointment_slot_id`). Attempting to book a slot that is already booked is physically rejected by the database engine and returns an HTTP `409 Conflict`.\n- **Doctor-Slot Ownership**: Validates that `slot.doctor_id == doctor_id` before acquiring a lock; cross-doctor booking attempts return HTTP `400 Bad Request`.\n- **Temporal Validity**: Validates that `slot.start_time` is in the future; past slots return HTTP `400 Bad Request`.\n- **Atomic State Transitions**: Inside a single database transaction, the slot status transitions from `AVAILABLE` to `BOOKED`, the appointment row is created with server-enforced initial status `CONFIRMED`, and an `AuditEvent` is generated. If an error occurs, the entire transaction rolls back.\n- **Cancellation & Slot Release**: Cancelling an appointment sets status to `CANCELLED` and safely reverts the slot status back to `AVAILABLE`.\n- **Audit Trail**: Every booking, cancellation, visit completion, follow-up recommendation, and workflow exception records an immutable row in `audit_events`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. AI Tool Interface Readiness (Section 9)\n\nTyped Python service functions are exposed with restricted signatures:\n\n1. `search_doctors_tool(db, specialty_or_department, hospital_id)`:\n   - Returns structured physician identifiers, names, specialties, and department names. Pure read-only query.\n2. `get_available_slots_tool(db, doctor_id, requested_date, time_range)`:\n   - Returns confirmed open slots with optional date and time window filters (`morning`, `afternoon`, `evening`).\n3. `book_appointment_tool(db, patient_reference, doctor_id, selected_slot_id, reason_category)`:\n   - Executes atomic booking with server-controlled initial status (`CONFIRMED`). Does not allow external models to pass arbitrary status or bypass validation.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Verification and Execution Status\n\n- **Code Actually Executed and Tested**:\n  - `python3 -m pip install -r backend/requirements.txt` installed FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.1, Pydantic 2.14, Alembic, and Pytest.\n  - `python3 backend/scripts/seed_data.py --reset` executed successfully, populating Aarogya One Hospital, 5 departments, 6 doctors, 36 future slots, 3 appointments, and 3 lab orders.\n  - `PYTHONPATH=backend pytest backend/tests/ -v` executed and **passed 26 out of 26 tests in 0.76 seconds**.\n  - TypeScript frontend compiled with **zero errors**.\n- **Commands to Run Locally**:\n  ```bash\n  # 1. Install dependencies\n  pip install -r backend/requirements.txt\n\n  # 2. Seed synthetic database\n  python3 backend/scripts/seed_data.py --reset\n\n  # 3. Run automated tests\n  PYTHONPATH=backend pytest backend/tests/ -v\n\n  # 4. Start FastAPI server\n  python3 -m uvicorn app.main:app --app-dir backend --port 8000 --reload\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Strict Scope Compliance & Remaining Blockers for Phase 2\n\n- **Intentionally Excluded in Phase 1 (Per Brief)**:\n  - No live Gnani Prisma speech-to-text integration (scheduled for Phase 2).\n  - No live Timbre text-to-speech integration (scheduled for Phase 2).\n  - No Evon model reasoning API calls or external credit usage.\n  - No clinical medical records (EMR) or clinical lab results.\n- **Ready for Next Phase**: The backend foundation, database schemas, transactional slot booking, and typed AI tool interfaces are ready for the reasoning model and voice pipeline integration."
    thinking: "**Verifying Project Scope**\n\nI\'m meticulously reviewing the initial user requirements. The focus now is ensuring complete alignment with the project brief\'s scope, specifically for Phase 1: Backend Foundation and Database. Every element will be double-checked to confirm the design meets specifications before moving forward.\n\n\n**Structuring Backend Framework**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the architectural design. I\'ve mapped out a modular backend structure for the Aarogya One project. Key components include the main application file, configurations, database interactions (models and sessions), and dedicated service layers for doctors, appointments, labs, and workflows. I\'m building APIs and schemas to handle the workflows. Finally, I\'m ensuring rigorous testing and data seeding for a complete backend framework.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the core data structures. The focus is now on meticulously crafting the database schema, including the Hospital, Department, Doctor, AppointmentSlot, Appointment, LabOrder, WorkflowException, and AuditEvent tables. I\'m ensuring all relationships and constraints are correctly established, and that the schema reflects all key fields as well as proper synthetic data. I\'m building data for hospital records, appointments, lab orders, and other workflows.\n\n\n**Developing API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core API endpoints. I\'ve designed routes for hospitals, doctors (with filtering), and appointment management, including booking, cancellation, and completion. I\'m focusing on GET and POST requests, including comprehensive error handling. I\'m taking booking reliability seriously, making sure the code is transaction-safe and has database-level protection against double booking.\n\n\n"
