10 tests: atomic booking, double booking rejection, cancel, follow-up\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 test_lab_orders.py          # 4 tests: status transitions, validation rejection\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 test_workflow.py            # 4 tests: deterministic detection, assignment, resolution\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 scripts/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 seed_data.py                # Idempotent synthetic seeder for Aarogya One Hospital\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 alembic/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 env.py, script.py.mako\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 versions/0001_initial_schema.py  # Migration establishing all 8 tables & constraints\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 alembic.ini, requirements.txt, .env.example, README.md\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/App.tsx                     # Interactive Developer & Architecture Verification Portal\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Database Schema & Booking Invariants\n\n- **Anti-Double Booking**: The `appointments` table enforces a database-level unique constraint on `slot_id` (`uq_appointment_slot_id`). Attempting to book a slot that is already booked is physically rejected by the database engine and returns an HTTP `409 Conflict`.\n- **Doctor-Slot Ownership**: Validates that `slot.doctor_id == doctor_id` before acquiring a lock; cross-doctor booking attempts return HTTP `400 Bad Request`.\n- **Temporal Validity**: Validates that `slot.start_time` is in the future; past slots return HTTP `400 Bad Request`.\n- **Atomic State Transitions**: Inside a single database transaction, the slot status transitions from `AVAILABLE` to `BOOKED`, the appointment row is created with server-enforced initial status `CONFIRMED`, and an `AuditEvent` is generated. If an error occurs, the entire transaction rolls back.\n- **Cancellation & Slot Release**: Cancelling an appointment sets status to `CANCE