  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s prompt regarding file modifications. My primary goal is to ensure a thorough understanding of the existing implementation before suggesting changes. The requirement to summarize both the current state and intended modifications is a key aspect I need to incorporate. I\'m carefully designing my response to meet this.\n\n\n**Reviewing System Components**\n\nI\'ve been examining the existing architecture in detail. The SQLAlchemy models and database constraints are clear, and I\'ve reviewed the tools for doctor searching, slot availability, and booking. The APIs are also well-defined, and their structure provides me with a basis. I\'m focusing on how these components integrate to fulfill user requests efficiently.\n\n\n**Evaluating API Coverage**\n\nI\'m now assessing the testing coverage of the API endpoints, specifically `/api/v1/lab-orders` and `/api/v1/workflow`. The 26 existing tests provide a strong baseline, and I\'m keen to determine if they adequately validate the functionality of these specific endpoints in the context of the user\'s intended modifications. I\'ll need to identify any gaps in the testing suite.\n\n**Addressing Phase 2 Needs**\n\nI\'m transitioning my focus to Phase 2, which involves implementing a `ConversationManager`. I\'m working to fully understand its responsibilities, including managing multi-turn conversations through a state machine, prompting for missing information such as doctor details and booking confirmations, all via the `session_id`.\n\n\n**Designing Adapter Components**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the architectural components for the reasoning adapter. I\'m focusing on `BaseReasoningAdapter`, its `process_turn` function, and the pluggable design for flexibility. I\'m building a concrete `MockReasoningAdapter` which focuses on understanding patient intent, and generating structured actions. The lack of tool-calling support is a significant point. Also, I\'m thinking about the restricted tool router and confirmation.\n\n\n**Confirming Booking Flow**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the booking confirmation process. Once all booking parameters are collected, I transition into the `AWAITING_CONFIRMATION` state. The agent summarizes the appointment details clearly, requesting explicit confirmation from the patient before executing the `book_appointment_tool`. Only an affirmative response triggers the booking. I will report on success only after the backend database commits the transaction. I\'m also planning the new API endpoints, specifically `/api/v1/agent/chat` and `/api/v1/agent/session`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_421021"
      name: "manage_task"
      arguments_json: "{\"Action\":\"status\",\"TaskId\":\"e3fc6292-c23a-4347-a298-15d68e50e6d9/task-213\",\"toolAction\":\"Checking dependency installation status\",\"toolSummary\":\"Check dependency install status\"}"
