      cascade_id: "e3fc6292-c23a-4347-a298-15d68e50e6d9"
    }
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Continue the existing MediVoice AI project from the completed Phase 1 checkpoint. Do not rebuild the database, rewrite working backend services, or remove existing tests.\nImplement Phase 2: Text-First AI Agent.\nInspect the current project structure and identify the existing search_doctors_tool, get_available_slots_tool, and book_appointment_tool.\nBuild a conversation manager that accepts patient messages, maintains conversation context, and asks for missing booking details.\nAdd a reasoning-model adapter with a clean interface so the model provider can be changed later. Do not assume Gnani AI or Evon supports tool calling until verified.\nImplement a restricted tool router exposing only the existing, allowlisted backend tools. The model must never access the database directly.\nRequire explicit patient confirmation before booking. Validate all arguments and availability on the backend, use the existing transactional booking service, and report success only after the database confirms the booking.\nAdd tests for doctor search, slot discovery, missing details, invalid tool arguments, booking confirmation, unavailable slots, and successful booking.\nPreserve the existing API contracts and all Phase 1 functionality. Run the available tests and TypeScript checks, and report the actual results.\nUse a mock reasoning adapter initially if live model integration is not yet verified. Do not integrate speech APIs or consume AI credits in this phase.\nBefore changing files, summarize the existing implementation and the specific files you plan to modify."
    items {
      text: "Continue the existing MediVoice AI project from the completed Phase 1 checkpoint. Do not rebuild the database, rewrite working backend services, or remove existing tests.\nImplement Phase 2: Text-First AI Agent.\nInspect the current project structure and identify the existing search_doctors_tool, get_available_slots_tool, and book_appointment_tool.\nBuild a conversation manager that accepts patient messages, maintains conversation context, and asks for missing booking details.\nAdd a reasoning-model adapter with a clean interface so the model provider can be changed later. Do not assume Gnani AI or Evon supports tool calling until verified.\nImplement a restricted tool router exposing only the existing, allowlisted backend tools. The model must never access the database directly.\nRequire explicit patient confirmation before booking. Validate all arguments and availability on the backend, use the existing transactional booking service, and report success only after the database confirms the booking.\nAdd tests for doctor search, slot discovery, missing details, invalid tool arguments, booking confirmation, unavailable slots, and successful booking.\nPreserve the existing API contracts and all Phase 1 functionality. Run the available tests and TypeScript checks, and report the actual results.\nUse a mock reasoning adapter initially if live model integration is not yet verified. Do not integrate speech APIs or consume AI credits in this phase.\nBefore changing files, summarize the existing implementation and the specific files you plan to modify."
    }
  }
}
