  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s prompt. I need to fully understand the instruction to summarize the existing implementation and planned file modifications *before* altering any files. This is a critical step to ensure I meet their expectations and work accurately.\n\n\n**Reviewing Current Implementation**\n\nI\'ve been reviewing the existing code base. I\'ve noted the SQLAlchemy models in `backend/app/models/`, focusing on `Hospital`, `Department`, `Doctor`, and the booking reliability measures. Key functionalities include tools for searching doctors, retrieving available slots, and booking appointments, accessible via existing APIs.\n\n\n**Examining Test Coverage**\n\nI\'m now diving into the existing test suite located in `backend/tests/`. I\'ve discovered a comprehensive set of 26 tests which validate various facets of the application\'s functionality. The tests cover doctor retrieval, booking logic (including invariants), lab orders, and workflow intelligence. This review will guide my integration efforts with the new workflow.\n\n\n**Defining Conversational Flow**\n\nI\'m working on the conversational flow between the user and system. The design includes a pluggable architecture, so I\'m implementing a `MockReasoningAdapter` which understands patient intents like booking, searching, and cancellations. This uses structured actions like `call_tool`, `ask_user`, and `confirm_booking` for clarity.\n\n\n**Designing Confirmation Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the booking confirmation flow. I\'ve designed it to summarize booking details clearly and prompt the patient for explicit confirmation (\"Would you like me to confirm this booking for...?\"). Only an affirmative response triggers the booking tool. Otherwise, the booking is either aborted or adjusted before any database updates. Success will be reported only after a successful database commit. I\'m also planning the new API endpoints and tests.\n\n\n"
    provider_assigned_message_id: "jBTNaqJK__TPsg_WpuVp"
  }
}
